nt to your interest in assurance case notations.\r\n*   **Ontology Components:** Understanding the building blocks of ontologies [source:8l364ov59pvnuklqi6mw] seems to be an element of your work, especially given the limitations of existing cybersecurity ontologies (like UCO) that have been noted in the SotA documents.\r\n*   **Assurance Case Notations \u2013 SAFER AUTONOMOUS SYSTEMS:** Exploration of other assurance case notations and how they can be used to automate AC construction processes [source:d8g923yj88wwg8k1t8nd].\r\n*   **energies-14-06862-v2.pdf:** Investigating the development of a security requirements model for smart grids [source:kd2h3ug9t6hb9tsslwid] as a use case that may inform your own modelling approaches.\r\n\r\n**Current Focus & Next Steps (Implied):**\r\nBased on the materials, your current focus appears to be:\r\n*   Evaluating the applicability of assurance case notations (particularly CAE and SACM) to the domain of cybersecurity.\r\n*   Considering how to start with evidence to simplify the process and improve compatibility with Common Criteria.\r\n*   Addressing the limitations of existing cybersecurity ontologies (like UCO) and exploring alternative modeling approaches.\"": "The project explores streamlining cybersecurity standards management. Initial research on SciSpace revealed challenges with existing standards (overlaps, domain specificity, validation needs) and potential solutions like ontologies and metamodels.\n\nThe core idea is to adapt assurance case notations (inspired by safety domains), starting with evidence management and aiming for Common Criteria compatibility. Research includes examining SACM, CAE, ontology components, and related notations like those used for safer autonomous systems. A smart grid security requirements model is also being investigated as a potential use case. \n\nCurrent focus involves evaluating assurance case notations (SACM, CAE) for cybersecurity, focusing on evidence-based simplification and addressing limitations of existing ontologies like UCO."
